Socket-Stream

High-level IO abstraction for SOCK_STREAM sockets

This module provides an IO management wrapper for SOCK_STREAM sockets
(e.g. TCP/IP) intended to facilitate the implementation of protocols
over such a socket.  This frees the programmer from the minutiae of
handling partial data transfers and interrupts, and the complexity of
IO in general and sockets in particular.


INSTALLATION

To install this module, run the following commands:

	perl Makefile.PL
	make
	make test
	make install

SUPPORT AND DOCUMENTATION

After installing, you can find documentation for this module with the
perldoc command.

    perldoc Socket::Stream

You can also look for information at:

    RT, CPAN's request tracker (report bugs here)
        https://rt.cpan.org/NoAuth/Bugs.html?Dist=Socket-Stream

    CPAN Ratings
        https://cpanratings.perl.org/d/Socket-Stream

    Search CPAN
        https://metacpan.org/release/Socket-Stream


